# Git LFS: the binary assets of this project. Git cannot delta a texture, a model or a sound, so without LFS the repository grows by the whole
# file every time one is saved again. It needs Git LFS on the machine (`git lfs install`, once). Where it is not installed Git ignores these
# rules and stores the files as it always does, so nothing breaks: the history just carries them whole.
#
# The extensions are the binary ones of the engine's asset types, plus the interchange formats the importers read (a model, a font) that a
# project keeps beside the file they make. Text assets (.scn .fab .mat .pmat .pps .animator .director, the scripts) are left out on purpose:
# Git diffs and compresses them well, and a scene or a material you can read in a diff is worth more than the space.
# Keep the list equal to the engine's asset types: a spec (project-template-lfs.spec.ts) fails when a binary type is missing from it.

# Textures
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tga filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.dds filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.hdr filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.exr filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Audio
*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ogg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.opus filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webm filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Video
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.m4v filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ogv filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# 3D models: .mdl is the engine's own format (binary, already compressed); the others are what an artist imports from (.obj is text but easily tens of MB)
*.mdl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.obj filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gltf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.glb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Animation clips (binary)
*.anim filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Fonts: .font is what the editor bakes from a font file (binary, mostly the atlas pictures)
*.ttf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.otf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.woff filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.woff2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.font filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
